From 45e84ee30f78acf67ba79d6200b988630c6a8244 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 09:17:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] conninfra, gen4m: do not depend on a modular modem driver

With the T880 kernel building the vendor CCCI modem driver as modules
(CONFIG_MTK_ECCCI_DRIVER=m), conninfra's MT6897 EMI code calls the modem
driver's shared memory lookup and gen4m enables its CCCI support. The
connectivity modules load at boot, while the modem modules are loaded by
hand during the modem bring-up: a dependency would load the modem driver
at boot (and the out-of-tree build does not see its header).

conninfra uses the lookup only with a built-in modem driver (the MCIF
area stays "not supported", as before); the build passes
CONFIG_MTK_WIFI_CCCI_SUPPORT=n to gen4m (CFG_MTK_CCCI_SUPPORT=0, as
before).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../conninfra/conn_drv/connv2/platform/mt6897/mt6897_emi.c  | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/connectivity/conninfra/conn_drv/connv2/platform/mt6897/mt6897_emi.c b/connectivity/conninfra/conn_drv/connv2/platform/mt6897/mt6897_emi.c
index d87553d..53aec02 100644
--- a/connectivity/conninfra/conn_drv/connv2/platform/mt6897/mt6897_emi.c
+++ b/connectivity/conninfra/conn_drv/connv2/platform/mt6897/mt6897_emi.c
@@ -74,7 +74,11 @@ void consys_emi_get_md_shared_emi_mt6897(phys_addr_t* base, unsigned int* size)
 	int ret = 0;
 
 #ifndef CONFIG_FPGA_EARLY_PORTING
-#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_MTK_ECCCI_DRIVER)
+/*
+ * Only with a built-in modem driver: conninfra loads at boot and must not
+ * pull in the modem driver modules, which are loaded by hand.
+ */
+#if IS_BUILTIN(CONFIG_MTK_ECCCI_DRIVER)
 	mdPhy = get_smem_phy_start_addr(MD_SYS1, SMEM_USER_RAW_MD_CONSYS, &ret);
 #else
 	pr_info("[%s] ECCCI Driver is not supported.\n", __func__);
-- 
2.55.0

